WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:14.030
<i>DOKI - Chihiro</i>

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:14.030
<i>DOKI</i>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.870
<b>fukigenna tenki moyou ga nori utsutteta aitsu</b>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.870
<b>不機嫌な天気模様が乗り移ってたアイツ</b>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.870
<b>That fellow was affected by bad weather</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>nanda! chotto naname ni sora wo miteta dake ka</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>なんだ！　ちょっとナナメに空を見てただけか</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:27.040
<b>What! He's only squinting at the sky</b>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.630
<b>shiritai (misetai)</b>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.630
<b>知りたい（見せたい）</b>

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.630
<b>I want to know (I want to see)</b>

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.210
<b>wakaritai (wakaranai)</b>

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.210
<b>解りたい（解らない）</b>

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.210
<b>I want to understand (I can't understand)</b>

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.800
<b>nakitai (nakenai)</b>

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.800
<b>泣きたい（泣けない）</b>

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.800
<b>I want to cry (I can't cry)</b>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.380
<b>soredemo</b>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.380
<b>それでも</b>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.380
<b>Even so,</b>

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.970
<b>shikatanai (kubomanai)</b>

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.970
<b>仕方ない（凹まない）</b>

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.970
<b>It can't be helped (Not feeling depressed)</b>

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.590
<b>itakunai (youkumonai)</b>

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.590
<b>痛くない（痒くもない）</b>

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.590
<b>It doesn't hurt (It doesn't itch)</b>

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.970
<b>kowashitai (kowaretai)</b>

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.970
<b>壊したい（壊れたい）</b>

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.970
<b>I want to break (I want to be broken)</b>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.640
<b>yuzurenai omoi nara</b>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.640
<b>譲れない思いなら</b>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.640
<b>I don't want to surrender these feelings</b>

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.400
<b>chiratsuku kiiro shingou mushishite</b>

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.400
<b>ちらつく黄色信号　無視して</b>

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.400
<b>Just ignore that flashing yellow signal</b>

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:53.030
<b>kou kakudo de joushou chuu kokoro no flying saucer</b>

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:53.030
<b>高角度で上昇中　心のflying saucer</b>

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:53.030
<b>The flying saucer in my heart is rising at a sharp angle</b>

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.870
<b>nakanaka sunao ni nan nai himitsu no tobira ni keri irete!</b>

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.870
<b>なかなか素直になんない秘密のトビラに蹴り入れて！</b>

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.870
<b>It kicks open that dishonest, secret door</b>

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.080
<b>chuugaeri de mata modotte kuru yo</b>

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.080
<b>宙返りでまた戻ってくるよ</b>

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.080
<b>Do a loop-the-loop and return once more {Loop-the-Loop is the title of this song}</b>

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>sakaraenai jiryoku mitai na omoi yo todoke!</b>

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>逆らえない磁力みたいな思いよ　届け！</b>

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>Convey those seemingly irresistable magnetic feelings to you!</b>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:19.180
<b>omote no kādo de shoubu shinai nande</b>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:19.180
<b>表のカードで勝負しないなんで</b>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:19.180
<b>You can't use a face card to decide the victory.</b>

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.060
<b>dare no tame no moraru?</b>

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.060
<b>誰のためのモラル？</b>

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.060
<b>Whose morals are those?</b>

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.950
Motto To LOVE-Ru 28

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.950
<u>Pollen Telepathy</u>

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.820
All right, I'm off.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.820
Take care!

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.410
Be careful, Celine.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.200
All right, let's go.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.660
Come here, come here!

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.460
It's not like I really care if you don't!

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.260
Eh? Isn't that Kotegawa?

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:03.850
I see.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.390
You're showing her the town.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.400
Oh yeah, wasn't she originally a flower growing in the garden?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:10.940
Yeah.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.030
But it really surprised me.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:17.030
Who would've thought that she would become human-like?

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.660
The universe really lacks common sense.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.790
What is it?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.540
It seems like she likes you, Kotegawa.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.170
R-Really?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.540
Oh my!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.840
Are you having a walk with your Papa and Mama? How nice!

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.880
Papa? Mama?!

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.260
<i>I'm back!</i>

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.720
<i>I'm home, Yui!</i>

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.930
<i>Ah, Celine.</i>

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.930
<i>Have you been a good girl?</i>

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.900
<i>Welcome home, darling.</i>

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.940
<i>Would you like dinner?</i>

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.440
<i>Or a bath first?</i>

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.280
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.950
<i>Before that, how about a welcome home kiss?</i>

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.540
Who would do that with this kind of person?!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.160
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:12.920
Eh?

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.040
Where's Celine-chan?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.550
She's gone! Oh crap... Where did she go?

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.050
Hey!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.260
Miss, you can't do that! {TLC komaru: troublesome?}

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.550
Celine, what are you doing?!

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.310
Sorry! I'll pay for it!

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.390
Sorry about that, Kotegawa.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.940
I'll pay you back next time.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.770
Don't worry.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.360
It's only a drink. {TLC did she say juice?}

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.480
But even though she's a plant, she can drink Coke...

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.820
Well, that's because Lala has been giving her all kinds of things for a long time.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:46.700
What's wrong?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.960
What? Is she drunk?

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.790
Eh? From Coke?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.420
Wait!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.560
Tenjouin-senpai!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.730
Oh, it's Yuuki Rito.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.770
What's the matter?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:16.690
What's that?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.940
P-Pollen?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.150
Wait, Celine!

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.610
Yuuki Rito...

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.080
I love you!

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.670
Ouch...

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.210
T-Tenjouin-senpai!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.380
Yuuki Rito...

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.640
Here. Understand...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.940
...this fast heartbeat...

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.200
Please...

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.030
Please do something more to me! {TLC: um not sure about this one}{gamma- not sure what to put for this, I tried to TL by transcribing and using a dictionary and I got something like "Please don't think I'm an innocent person, or "Please don't treat me like I'm innocent." but that's obviously a very rough translation that is suggesting something more (mujaki = innocence) Well I decided to change it to this... he already made her heartbeat fast so this is suggestive of what else he can do. I thought "mess me up" sounded weird}

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:13.410
What are you doing?!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.710
I'm saved...

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.920
Y-Yuuki Rito!

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.260
Wait up!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.310
Crap!

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.350
Where did you go, Celine?

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.740
What the hell is going on?!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.950
Maybe it's because of Celine's pollen?

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.030
Probably...

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.540
If I don't catch her quick...

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.200
Yuuki-kun!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.830
Hug me!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.520
Yuuki-kun! Hug me!{no clue where this has to go?! -masat}

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.560
This is great!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.690
Eh?

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.150
What... were we doing?

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.240
Yuuki-kun...

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.330
Eh?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.580
I see.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.620
So something like that happened.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.790
Why did this have to happen to me...

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:50.050
It seems like when Celine-san is drunk, she emits a special pollen.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:55.510
That pollen makes the victim fall in love with Rito-san for a short period of time.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.180
Why only Rito?

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:03.810
I think it's because Celine-san likes Rito-san a lot, so this feeling is transferred to the victim.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.360
W-What's up with that ability?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.820
How shameless.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.880
Motto To LOVE-Ru 29

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:22.880
<u>A Girl's Feelings {TLC}</u>

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.460
Ah! It's Run-chan!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.120
Did you know?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.170
She'll be singing a new song with Magical Girl Kyouko-chan!

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.170
Eh?

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.710
She's working hard.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.720
Isn't it nice, Run-chan?

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.930
You made friends with Kyouko-chan...

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.810
If we don't get home quickly with our shopping, Mikan will be upset. {Or: Mikan won't be pleased? Mikan is too kawaii to get angry}

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.270
Right.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.060
Oh yeah, Lala-sama...

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.770
Isn't Magical Girl Kyouko airing today? {TLC: broadcast?}

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.520
Oh no! I forgot!

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.400
You're hopeless.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.990
You go home first.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:51.900
Are you sure?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:52.990
Yep.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.240
Thanks, Rito!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.450
I love you!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.250
All right, take care of the rest! {TLC: yoroshiku: never know how to TL this lol}

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.130
Hey, it's not a problem, right?

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.960
Hang out with me for a bit...

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.670
You're annoying.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.840
I have no interest in careless men like you. {TLC: Frivolous?}

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.840
Don't say that...

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.060
Ah! Darling!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.190
You're so late! {TLC: or late?}

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.110
Momioka! What's up?!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.200
Hurry. Let's go! {Let's go quickly}

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.200
Hey! I've got plans...

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.070
I see...

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.870
Shit. She already has a boyfriend.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.910
You're a lifesaver!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.330
What on earth was going on?

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.000
I was being hit on by a persistent, dirty man.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.500
It was a real pain.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.670
Thank you, Yuuki.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.970
No problem.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.630
All right, I'll be off then.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.850
Wait.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.520
Let me return the favour for saving me.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.780
Welcome back!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.490
Eh? Risa.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.620
You're with Yuuki?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.370
How unusual.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.160
S-Sawada! What're you doing, dressed like that?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.620
Are you surprised?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.540
Well, Mio just likes things like this.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.670
That's right.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.090
Enjoy your stay, O~ni~i~chan~

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.050
Onii-chan...

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.220
Well, it's <i>that</i>  kind of shop after all. {TLC}

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.350
So, eat up! It's on me.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.810
Thanks.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:50.060
But I never imagined that the day I'd go on a date with you would come, Yuuki. {TLC}

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.820
But this isn't really a date, right?

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.820
Are you saying that dating me is bad?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.740
I didn't mean it like that...

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.830
Yuuki...

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.710
Truthfully, how far have you gone with Lala-chi?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.920
What're you talking about?!

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.920
Judging from that reaction, not very far, eh?

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.720
What a waste. {TLC}

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.800
As you live under the same roof, you should be able to do anything.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.850
Anything?

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:34.110
Lala-chi is a good girl, but she acts like a kid.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.530
You have to take the lead... {TLC}

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.150
...in heart and body.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.570
Heart and body...

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:43.660
Yep.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.290
Heart... and body...

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.250
Stop saying weird stuff!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.710
You're so funny!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.510
Oh. I didn't realize that it already got so dark! {TLC}

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.300
You're right.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.060
All right, I'm going home.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.600
Thanks for the meal.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.770
You're going to let a girl walk home alone in the dark?

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.650
Walk me home!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.940
What?

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.740
We're not at your house yet?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.620
A bit further, just a bit further.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:41.720
Why of all routes do we have to walk through this one?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.340
Because it's a short cut!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.350
We've arrived!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.310
This is my house.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.530
All right, I'm...

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.230
Wait.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.700
Since you're here, come inside for a bit.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.120
I'll serve you some coffee.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.080
No thanks, I'm-

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.290
This is my room.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.840
So, come in.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.630
O-Okay.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.840
There seems to be no one else at home. {TLC}

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:34.310
My parents are out at work, and they come home late.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:37.230
I-I see.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.070
All right, I'm-

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.240
There's no need... {TLC}

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.120
...to hold back so much.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:56.830
Weren't you also excited{dokidoki} when we were walking on that road earlier?

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.960
M-Momioka!

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.180
I've also neglected those feelings...

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:12.310
...and sometimes I have lonely nights too.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.400
It'll be all right.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.520
I will teach you carefully... {TLC}

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.660
Before Lala-chi does...

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.740
Use me...

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.040
...for practice.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:45.470
N-No!{lol edit or shorten this to your needs -masat}

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.390
How cute!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.930
Is that really a guy's reaction?

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.730
You didn't get into the mood or anything!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.190
Geez...

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.530
She actually said "Thanks for helping me kill time!" {TLC}

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.030
How dare she make fun of me.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:11.740
It's from Momioka...

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.330
Inbox

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.330
Momioka Risa

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.330
Dear Darling,

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.330
If you ever get enough courage, 
come and see 
me any time!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:17.330
- Risa -

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.910
Dear Darling~

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.540
If you ever get enough courage, come and see me any time!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.330
Risa.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.590
She's just making fun of me, right?

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.670
So? Where's the shopping?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:25.760
Ah!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.840
Eh? Rito, you're so late!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.390
Did you wander off somewhere?

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.730
I'm sorry, Lala!

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:03.000
Motto To LOVE-Ru 30

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:03.000
<u>Doki Doki Mail</u>

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.750
Kotegawa!

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.550
What do you want, Yuuki-kun?

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:13.220
Hey, do you know about a fantasy novel called "A Midnight Date?"

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.850
The one where the main character is a cat.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.350
Yeah. I'm reading that book right now.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.560
Ah, so you like cats.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.730
Actually, I'm looking for it because my dad's work needs that book for reference.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.320
All the bookstores are sold out.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:30.740
When you've finished reading it, could you please lend it to me?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.700
Because of that, it must be urgent then.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.870
All right. If it's like that, I'll lend it to you.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.370
You sure?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.710
I don't read it much anyway.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.130
Yes! Thank you!

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.000
All right, let me know when you're finished with it.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.880
I'll give you my e-mail. {TLC mail = e-mail?}

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.710
E-mail?

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.600
I didn't think I'd finish it so quickly.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.560
I wonder if I should tell Yuuki-kun right away.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:09.940
It's the weekend. If it's urgent, he can come over and pick it up tomorrow.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.120
Now that I think about it,

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:22.160
apart from family, this is the first time that I'm sending e-mail to a guy.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.460
This is only a normal way of communication.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:28.420
It's not shameless or anything.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:34.800
I finished reading. 
Come and get it right now.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.600
No!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.260
No matter how I look at it, this is just too rude.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.940
Good evening. 
What are you doing right now? 
I've been thinking about you...

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:45.900
What?!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.360
This sounds like I'm his lover...

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.730
I have to sound more natural.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.860
Like I said, it's not like that!

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.990
Sending

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.750
I've wasted 30 minutes thinking about how to write this e-mail.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:05.500
I guess I'll take a bath...

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.750
Stop right there!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.590
Who are you?

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.630
It's about time you asked!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:15.510
I'm Magical Girl Kyouko!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.350
Go for it, Kyouko-chan!

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.680
Sis...

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.770
I want to watch the animal show. {TLC}

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.650
Rito-san has such a cute sleeping face.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.360
Eh?

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.190
Rito-san!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:35.820
You've got mail!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.700
Momo. Answer it for me.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.410
Is that all right?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.540
I'm so tired from weeding the garden today.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.500
It's probably from Saruyama anyway. Thanks.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.170
Ah... All right.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.050
Eh? It's from Kotegawa-san.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.800
Good evening.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.510
The Midnight Date was good.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:04.640
Since you said you wanted it, no matter what, I'm giving it to you.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.390
Take good care of it.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.230
M-Midnight date?!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.150
"Giving it...?"

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.650
What exactly did you give Rito-san, Kotegawa-san?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.440
<i>Yuuki-kun.</i>

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:20.320
<i>Since you said you wanted it, no matter what, I'm giving it to you.</i>

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.200
<i>Take good care of it.</i>

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.080
I wonder how I should reply to this?

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.670
I wonder if Yuuki-kun has read the e-mail yet?

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.720
I hope he doesn't think it's weird.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.050
He replied!

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.270
Thanks!

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.310
I'm really happy about how you feel.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.820
This is a secret between the two of us.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:57.070
Eh? A secret between the two of us?

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.910
What is he saying? Geez...

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:06.160
Who would've thought that the honest Kotegawa-san would...

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.580
I've always wondered why she was looking at Rito-san differently.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:11.460
Momo!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.340
Sis has gone into the bath first.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.130
What're you doing?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.840
That's Rito's mobile phone, right?

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:23.260
Yeah, Rito-san asked me to reply to Kotegawa-san's e-mail.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.680
To Kotegawa?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.810
Good timing! I've got something to ask her as well.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.230
Give it to me for a sec. {Give?}

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:33.270
Hey, don't do that, Nana! You don't have permission...

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.570
Geez...

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.030
What do you mean by a secret between the two of us?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.400
There's no need to make a big deal out of it.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.070
It's a secret between the two of us.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.200
Honestly.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.920
Ah, it's from Yuuki-kun again.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.630
What is it this time?

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:54.250
Huh?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:58.050
Kotegawa, I hope you'll keep this a secret.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.010
What is your opinion on small breasts?

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:03.590
Oops. I forgot to write my name before sending it.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.930
Oh dear.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:08.060
Kotegawa replied.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.390
Give it to me.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.600
Hey, what the hell do you mean?

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.600
Oh dear...

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.650
Momo, did you reply to the e-mail?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.690
Um...

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:23.240
It looks like we've made her angry... {TLC}

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.410
That Saruyama...

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.370
So short tempered...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.120
Rito, I've got a call from a friend.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.210
Can you help me do the washing up?

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.630
All right. I'll be there soon.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.380
I'm sorry, Momo, but can you send a follow up for me?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:41.380
You sure?

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.760
I'll leave it up to you. {TLC yoroshiku}

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.010
What should we do?

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:49.560
For now, we should explain that the e-mail just now was from Nana.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:51.180
Celine-san!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.900
Hey! That's not a toy!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.650
Wait!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.480
Gotcha!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.360
Sis!

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.120
That shutter sound just now...

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.200
Don't tell me...

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.080
Sent

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:15.540
This isn't good.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.710
I need to calm down first.

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:22.260
That e-mail might be Rito's idea of a joke.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:33.180
I always get angry at Yuuki-kun for no apparent reason.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.600
That's not good.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.150
All right. I'll reword my mail.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:40.730
Yuuki-kun?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:41.900
This isn't good... you sent one back first...

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.410
This is sexual harassment!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.200
So that's how it is.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.160
What happened afterwards?

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.420
Afterwards, let's apologize to Rito-san together, okay?

